{
 "encounter_id": "00905",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "CAREGIVER"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Sorry, sorry, we're late, I took the wrong turn, the sat nav sent us the long way round. This is Chloe, she fell off the trampoline about two hours ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "No worries. Hi Chloe, I'm Dr Nguyen. How are you feeling? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My arm hurts."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Which arm?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "This one. The left. Near my wrist. It's sore."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "She landed on it, I saw it. It was her left hand, flat out, and she screamed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Was anyone else on the trampoline? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Her cousin, Jack, but he'd got off. He's the one who ran in to get me, he's six. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's a good cousin. Chloe, does it look different?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It's puffy."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Can you turn your hand over for me, like you're holding soup?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ow. No. It hurts."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "She can't turn it over, no. She tried in the car."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Did you hit your head, Chloe?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Just my arm."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "She didn't hit her head. She was awake and crying straight away. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Did you feel dizzy, or pass out?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any tingling in your fingers?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit funny. No, not funny. Just sore."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "So no tingling? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No tingling."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Does your elbow or shoulder hurt?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, just by the wrist."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any medicines, Chloe's carer?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "She had ibuprofen, 200 mg, in the car, I keep it in my bag. And montelukast, 5 mg, every night for her asthma."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you. Any allergies, Chloe?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Egg. She's allergic to egg. But I couldn't tell you what happens, her mum would know."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's fine. Any medical history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Asthma, eczema, and hay fever."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "She had grommets when she was four."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Anything in the family?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Her mum has migraines, and her dad has asthma too."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Which grade are you in, Chloe?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Year four."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you play sport?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Netball. And the trampoline."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And who's at home?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Her mum, dad, and her little brother. I just look after her after school."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Okay. Let me check your vitals, Chloe. Pulse 104, blood pressure 100 over 62, temperature 36.9, oxygen 99 percent, breathing 20, and weight 29 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "All normal? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "All normal for her size. Chloe, I'm going to gently feel your arm, you tell me when it hurts.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "There. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There's swelling around the left wrist, and it's very tender over the end of the forearm bone."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ow! ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Sorry, Chloe. I can feel her pulse at the wrist, and her fingers are pink and warm."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Good, that's good. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any problem with your breathing today, Chloe, with your asthma?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, it's okay."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And any tummy ache or throwing up?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. I'm fine."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I think this looks like a broken wrist. A fracture of the forearm bone, near the wrist."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Oh no. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's very common in children, it heals well. I'd like to arrange an X-ray of the wrist and forearm, and an X-ray of the elbow too, to be safe."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Will it hurt? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Not at all, you just hold still. And I'd like to put her arm in a splint until then."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And I'd like to arrange a fracture clinic appointment for the cast."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "When would that be? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The nurse will book it before you leave. If her fingers turn blue or numb, or the pain gets much worse, come back straight away."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I will. Thank you, doctor. ~"
  }
